 result←object New arg;parent;name;where;newobj;props;border;nocaption;∆where;∆caption;∆border;at;ws;mdi;psize
 (parent name)←object ⍝ Separate non-standard two-part argument
 ⍝ Optionally prepend object defaults (in reverse order) to be handled
 (∆where ∆caption ∆border)←arg ##._supp.GetInitialProps'where' 'caption' 'border←' ⍝ Which of our defaults are they giving us anyway (so we can skip our defaults)

 mdi←parent ⎕VGET⊂'_Owner'⎕NULL
 :If 4≠≢∊∆where
     :If mdi≠⎕NULL
     :AndIf mdi._class≡'MDIForm'
         ⍝ We're creating this Form inside of an MDIForm.
         ⍝ In this case "parent" is the client window (Dyalog parent) and "mdi" is the MDIForm container (APL+Win parent)
         ⍝ When creating a Form inside of an MDIForm the placement of the new Form is not centered, it cascades every 26:26 pixels
⍝? Still need to figure out how to determine child Form sizes - formulas are not apparent
         at←mdi ⎕VGET⊂'_next_position'(0 0) ⋄ psize←mdi._Class._supp.ClientSize mdi
         where←at,ws←psize÷2 2 ⍝? Just guess at the new size for now
         :If ∨/psize≤ws+at←at+26 26÷⊃##._supp.MyUnits mdi ⋄ at←0 0 ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ Where should the next one go? ⍝? Check formula for overflow detection
         mdi._next_position←at ⍝ Keep track of where our next default starting location will be (wrap-around on overflow)
         arg,⍨←⊂'where'where ⍝ [2] Start us with a default 'where' size and position (APL+Win measure) -- will usually be overridden later
     :Else
         where←,parent._size÷⍤1⊢2 2⍴4 4 2 2 ⍝ Default APL+Win Form size and position ⍝? Does this give us the right data for scale=0?
         arg,⍨←⊂'where'where ⍝ [2] Start us with a default 'where' size and position (APL+Win measure) -- will usually be overridden later
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
 arg,⍨←(~arg ##._supp.HasInitialProps'caption')/⊂'caption'name ⍝ [1] Use the object name as a default caption
 border←+/∆border,(0=≢∆border)/_border ⍝ Assume default, and handle multi-bit borders

 :If mdi=⎕NULL ⋄ :AndIf parent._class≡'System' ⍝ If this is a top-level object, then create it as a Form
     props←'Form'('Visible' 0)
 :Else ⍝ Otherwise it's in an MDIForm and this is going to be a SubForm
     props←'SubForm'('Visible' 0)
 :EndIf
 nocaption←∆caption≡'' ⍝ (This won't match a ⍬ default, thus it's been provided this way)
 :If nocaption∧16>+/border ⍝ No border; no title bar
     props,←('Sizeable' 0)('Moveable' 0)('SysMenu' 0)('MinButton' 0)('MaxButton' 0)('Border' 0)
 :ElseIf nocaption∧1∊border ⍝ Thin border; no title bar
     props,←('Sizeable' 0)('Moveable' 0)('SysMenu' 0)('MinButton' 0)('MaxButton' 0)('Border' 1)
 :Else ⍝ Normal border and title bar
     props,←(16 32 64∊border),¨⍨⊂¨'SysMenu' 'MinButton' 'MaxButton'
     props,←('Sizeable' 1)('Moveable' 1)('Border' 1)
 :EndIf

 newobj←⎕VGET(parent⍕⍛,'.',name)##.##.∆WC props ⍝ Create the actual Dyalog object
 result←parent newobj ##.##.New.Initialize arg ⍝ Complete standard class-initialization procedure
